      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "First, distribute \\(2x\\) across the second term \\((x+5)\\):\n\\[\n(2x+3)(x+5) = 2x \\cdot x + 2x \\cdot 5 + 3 \\cdot x + 3 \\cdot 5\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n2x \\cdot x = 2x^2\n\\]\n\\[\n2x \\cdot 5 = 10x\n\\]\n\\[\n3 \\cdot x = 3x\n\\]\n\\[\n3 \\cdot 5 = 15\n\\]\nCombining all these terms, we get:\n\\[\n2x^2 + 10x + 3x + 15 = 2x^2 + 13x + 15\n\\]\nTherefore, the expanded form of \\((2x+3)(x+5)\\) is \\(\\boxed{2x^2 + 13x + 15}\\).",
